        "original_id": "fa2678bf-55f6-5537-82ba-205df0a32ebc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: America Is Dying Slowly, Breakadawn, Buhloone Mindstate\n- Organizations: Red Hot Organization\n- People: De La Soul, Mobb Deep, Coolio, Biz Markie, Chubb Rock, The Lost Boyz, Pete Rock, Common, Wu-Tang Clan\n- Places: Long Island, New York\n- Concepts: Red Hot AIDS Benefit Series, AIDS\n\nFacts:\n- In 1987, De La Soul formed as an American hip hop trio on Long Island, New York.\n- In 1993, De La Soul released \"Breakadawn\" as a single from its third album \"Buhloone Mindstate\".\n- America Is Dying Slowly is a compilation album whose title is a backronym for AIDS.\n- America Is Dying Slowly is the eighth album in the Red Hot AIDS Benefit Series recorded by the Red Hot Organization.\n- America Is Dying Slowly featured collaborations from hip hop acts including De La Soul, Mobb Deep, Coolio, Biz Markie, Chubb Rock, The Lost Boyz, Pete Rock, Common, and Wu-Tang Clan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
